A DLL mod that gets you back on your feet much faster after dying: your death counts the moment the death animation starts, and the long pause on the "YOU DIED" screen is skipped. Toggle it on and off in-game with a hotkey.

[size=4][b]Why this mod?[/b][/size]
[i]Have you ever died to the same boss for the tenth time in a row, and then had to sit through your character slowly crumbling to the ground, followed by "YOU DIED" hanging on screen for what feels like forever - before you can even start the run back?

Yeah, me too. I've probably spent more time staring at that screen than at some of the bosses.

So I made this mod. The death animation still plays, but the game stops making you wait for it, and "YOU DIED" fades out right away. A normal death now gets you back to the grace in about 4 seconds instead of 12-14. More tries, less waiting.[/i]

[size=4][b]Features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Your death counts as soon as the death animation starts - the animation itself still plays.[/*]
[*]Skips the pause on the "YOU DIED" screen before it fades out.[/*]
[*]Respawn in about 4 seconds instead of 12-14 after a normal death.[/*]
[*]Doesn't replace any game files, so it works alongside animation mods and overhauls.[/*]
[*]Hotkey to toggle the mod on/off in-game, to compare with vanilla.[/*]
[*]Hotkey to reload the ini without restarting the game.[/*]
[/list]

[b][color=#E74C3C]Only use in offline mode with EAC disabled![/color][/b]

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]

Any DLL mod loader works, e.g. [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/eldenring/mods/117]Elden Mod Loader[/url], [url=https://github.com/soulsmods/ModEngine2/releases]Mod Engine 2[/url], [url=https://github.com/garyttierney/me3/releases]Mod Engine 3[/url].

[b]Option 1 - [url=https://github.com/soulsmods/ModEngine2/releases]Mod Engine 2[/url] (recommended)[/b]
[list=1]
[*]Download Mod Engine 2 from the link above and extract it into your game folder (the same folder as [i]eldenring.exe[/i]).[/*]
[*]Download this mod, then create a folder to hold it and its INI file - for example, inside your game folder create a [b]natives[/b] folder.[/*]
[*]Open [b]config_eldenring.toml[/b] and edit [b]external_dlls = [ ][/b] to add the DLL, e.g.:
[code]external_dlls = [
    "natives\FasterRevival.dll",
][/code]
[/*]
[*]Launch the game using Mod Engine 2's launcher, [b]modengine2_launcher.exe[/b].[/*]
[/list]

[b]Option 2 - [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/eldenring/mods/117]Elden Mod Loader[/url][/b]
[list=1]
[*]Download Elden Mod Loader from the link above and extract it into your game folder.[/*]
[*]Download this mod and drag [b]FasterRevival.dll[/b] and [b]FasterRevival.ini[/b] into the [b]mods[/b] folder.[/*]
[*]Launch the game - the mod will be loaded automatically.[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Credits[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Inspired by [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/eldenring/mods/3367]Faster Death Animation[/url] by 0-F and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/eldenring/mods/501]Faster Respawn[/url] by ImAxel0 ([url=https://github.com/ImAxel0/EldenRing-FasterRespawn-Mod]MIT[/url]) - same results, done at runtime instead of by editing game files or patching code.[/*]
[*]Game structures via [url=https://github.com/vswarte/fromsoftware-rs]fromsoftware-rs[/url].[/*]
[/list]

